{"text": "[Dreamy, longing] And that is one big thing Steve still needed to think about. Because at some point, Steve just wanted to go to bed. And let this whole team he had built do his work. Just this once: on the real data, with every check switched off, all night long.\n\n[Ominous, mock-dramatic] But when Steve left the room... a lot could go wrong. Everything the worker read flew out of the window, to the Worker Company, where its brain is. And the keys hung one step away. [short pause] And if they burned the house down... it was HIS house that burned down.\n\n[Thoughtful, a little wiser] So Steve came to the same conclusion as a lot of other people. Maybe it wasn't a good idea to have the workers in his own house. Maybe they needed another house to work in.\n\n[Brisk, like a cheerful salesman] Sometimes that's a virtual machine. Or a container. It doesn't need to be Docker, it can also be Podman. Or some kind of cloud, the online system, where they do it all for you.\n\n[Warm and cheeky] In there, only practice data. And a badge that opens one door, and expires. The keys stay at home. [deadpan] So if something burns over there... it isn't Steve's house.\n\n[Mock-serious lecture] Because there's one big difference between the two. Whatever the worker reads goes to the company. No spies needed: that's simply where its brain is. In your cellar, it can read just about everything in your house. In the other house... only what's inside that house.\n\n[Hushed, conspiratorial] And the company keeps it for a while. On a personal plan that allows training... for five years.\n\n[Warm and cheeky] So the other house is way better. Because Steve had a LOT of things he'd rather the company didn't know. From the office, only practice data leaves. On a company plan, it's kept thirty days, and not used for training. [short pause] Don't share your data if you don't need to.\n\n[Serious, steady, slowing down] Steve set up the office and the company plan last. [short pause] You should do it first.", "start": [0.0, 0.016, 0.018, 0.019, 0.021, 0.022, 0.024, 0.032, 0.04, 0.048, 0.05, 0.052, 0.054, 0.056, 0.059, 0.061, 0.064, 0.072, 0.08, 0.133, 0.187, 0.24, 0.32, 0.42, 0.52, 0.62, 0.72, 0.8, 0.96, 1.12, 1.28, 1.36, 1.44, 1.52, 1.6, 1.68, 1.76, 1.84, 1.92, 1.968, 2.016, 2.064, 2.112, 2.16, 2.24, 2.32, 2.4, 2.48, 2.56, 2.64, 2.8, 2.848, 2.896, 2.944, 2.992, 3.04, 3.16, 3.18, 3.2, 3.22, 3.24, 3.26, 3.28, 3.36, 3.4, 3.44, 3.52, 3.536, 3.552, 3.568, 3.584, 3.6, 3.68, 3.744, 3.808, 3.872, 3.936, 4.0, 4.56, 4.64, 4.674, 4.709, 4.743, 4.777, 4.811, 4.846, 4.88, 4.96, 5.0, 5.04, 5.12, 5.18, 5.24, 5.3, 5.36, 5.52, 5.552, 5.584, 5.616, 5.648, 5.68, 6.0, 6.16, 6.208, 6.256, 6.304, 6.352, 6.4, 6.48, 6.52, 6.56, 6.6, 6.64, 6.76, 6.78, 6.8, 6.82, 6.84, 6.86, 6.88, 6.92, 6.94, 6.96, 7.0, 7.02, 7.04, 7.12, 7.16, 7.2, 7.36, 7.413, 7.467, 7.52, 8.0, 8.08, 8.107, 8.133, 8.16, 8.24, 8.267, 8.293, 8.32, 8.44, 8.47, 8.5, 8.53, 8.56, 8.64, 8.688, 8.736, 8.784, 8.832, 8.88, 9.0, 9.03, 9.06, 9.09, 9.12, 9.2, 9.24, 9.28, 9.36, 9.387, 9.413, 9.44, 9.52, 9.568, 9.616, 9.664, 9.712, 9.76, 9.8, 9.82, 9.84, 9.92, 9.973, 10.027, 10.08, 10.24, 10.28, 10.32, 10.36, 10.4, 10.96, 11.04, 11.1, 11.16, 11.22, 11.28, 11.4, 11.43, 11.46, 11.49, 11.52, 11.6, 11.68, 11.76, 11.84, 11.92, 12.32, 12.4, 12.44, 12.48, 12.52, 12.533, 12.547, 12.56, 12.72, 12.78, 12.84, 12.9, 12.96, 13.04, 13.12, 13.2, 13.28, 13.36, 13.68, 13.84, 13.88, 13.92, 13.96, 14.0, 14.08, 14.128, 14.176, 14.224, 14.272, 14.32, 14.4, 14.432, 14.464, 14.496, 14.528, 14.56, 14.64, 14.68, 14.72, 14.76, 14.8, 14.84, 14.88, 14.92, 14.96, 15.04, 15.12, 15.2, 15.28, 15.68, 15.76, 15.787, 15.813, 15.84, 15.92, 15.952, 15.984, 16.016, 16.048, 16.08, 16.16, 16.22, 16.28, 16.34, 16.4, 16.68, 17.66, 17.66, 17.667, 17.673, 17.676, 17.678, 17.68, 17.682, 17.684, 17.687, 17.693, 17.7, 17.702, 17.703, 17.705, 17.707, 17.71, 17.713, 17.716, 17.718, 17.72, 17.722, 17.723, 17.725, 17.727, 17.733, 17.74, 17.793, 17.847, 17.9, 17.98, 18.0, 